WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.910
Let's talk a little bit about the stock market.

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:04.850
We have an impeached president here in the
United States.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.740
One of the predictions that Donald Trump made
many times in the lead up to his impeachment

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:13.530
was the markets will crash if you impeach
me.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:15.200
Now it turns out it didn't happen.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.140
Markets have actually been fine since Donald
Trump was impeached last Wednesday by the

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.630
house of representatives.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:26.570
A reminder, here's Donald Trump in September
when he quote, if they actually did this,

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:28.869
the markets would crash.

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:35.970
Do you think it was luck that got us to the
best stock market and economy in our history?

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.300
It wasn't.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.380
Now there's a few things that I think are
important to talk about here.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:47.980
First of all, the way the market is believed
to work supposedly works according to market

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:54.820
evangelists is that the market reflects all
known information at any point in time.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:01:00.140
So for example, when Donald Trump was impeached
last Wednesday, it makes sense that stocks

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:06.130
didn't move hugely on that news because it
was known that Donald Trump would be impeached

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:10.710
the previous week when it became clear that
the house judiciary would be voting to impeach.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:14.639
Knowing that Democrats control the house,
we actually learned well in advance of the

00:01:14.639 --> 00:01:19.320
actual vote in the house that there would
be an impeachment of the president.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.159
Case in point, when Nancy Pelosi first announced
the impeachment inquiry on September 24th

00:01:24.159 --> 00:01:29.229
the Dow actually did drop a few hundred points,
but then those losses were recovered and the

00:01:29.229 --> 00:01:33.610
stock market has actually occasionally hit
new highs since that day and we can debate

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:36.729
whether that matters, what that says about
the economy, who that affects.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:41.049
That doesn't change any of the sort of deeper
underlying economic questions around looking

00:01:41.049 --> 00:01:42.810
at the stock market.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:48.499
But increasingly there is this idea that actually
impeachment of a president of the United States

00:01:48.499 --> 00:01:53.299
when it is Trump specifically, it wouldn't
affect the economy that much.

00:01:53.299 --> 00:02:00.020
Now, of course, if the act of being impeached
throws Donald Trump into an erratic panic,

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:02.479
he could do something nutty that would affect
the economy.

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:05.559
He could make a rational decisions about trade
policy.

00:02:05.559 --> 00:02:10.500
For example, he could bomb a country, he could
start a military conflict or he's liable to

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:15.030
do a lot of different things that would move
the markets as soon as it is known that that

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:17.020
is something Trump is going to do.

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:22.110
But in terms of Trump's impeachment itself
and the hypothetical removal from the Senate,

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:25.540
even though of course it appears that he is
going to be acquitted when that Senate trial

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:33.620
ultimately happens, we have a known tax system,
for example, we have known regulatory infrastructure

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:40.209
trumps conviction or acquittal in the Senate,
uh, is not going to change those things in

00:02:40.209 --> 00:02:42.180
any direct way.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:47.349
It's actually possible that Trump's conviction
on impeachment, which would remove him, would

00:02:47.349 --> 00:02:52.670
maybe better relations with other countries,
even if it's totally wacky, ideological right-wing

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:55.900
Christian Mike Pence who were to replace Donald
Trump.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:59.959
It's hard to imagine a more cartoonish laughingstock
than Donald Trump when it comes to international

00:02:59.959 --> 00:03:00.959
relations.

00:03:00.959 --> 00:03:04.030
So, uh, believe me, I don't want Mike Pence
to be president.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:07.840
Even that I think could arguably be an improvement
in some sense.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:11.920
What the stock market doesn't like is a surprise.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:17.220
And so far Donald Trump's impeachment has
progressed in pretty predictable steps.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:22.209
Conviction is now a question Mark, but again,
presumably we will know in advance of the

00:03:22.209 --> 00:03:26.769
Senate vote whether there will or won't be
a conviction if half the country has been

00:03:26.769 --> 00:03:29.420
waiting for Trump to be impeached for years.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:34.629
It does make sense that it wouldn't move the
market that much if you believe in how the

00:03:34.629 --> 00:03:37.359
the, the market always assimilates known information.

00:03:37.359 --> 00:03:42.819
Um, then it was already part of the stock
market level, the desire and expectation and

00:03:42.819 --> 00:03:46.530
ultimately the realization that Trump would
be impeached would have already been priced

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:47.530
in.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:51.810
Now the bigger issues are of course the stock
market is not the economy.

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:57.560
A lot of people who just work for a living
their day to day is not guided by the stock

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:58.560
market.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:03:59.939
It is guided by what is cost of living.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.239
Uh, what are wages doing?

00:04:02.239 --> 00:04:04.810
What is going on economically in their state.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:10.000
The stock market may indeed be in a bubble
that's heading towards popping at some point.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.090
That's been said for a very long time.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:17.199
We have serious trade policy issues in the
country that are now hurting farmers and manufacturers

00:04:17.199 --> 00:04:18.639
in many States.

00:04:18.639 --> 00:04:21.579
Those don't look like they're going to be
resolved anytime soon.

00:04:21.579 --> 00:04:27.199
But the major conclusion here remains Trump's
presence in the white house is not the heart

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:32.830
of the stock market's success the way that
Donald Trump has claimed for awhile now, Trump's

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.680
predictions aren't particularly good.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:41.419
Trump's sense of self importance in the economy
is drastically overblown beyond his ability

00:04:41.419 --> 00:04:47.080
to actually hamper it via destructive trade
policy and ruining international alliances.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:51.479
Maybe these are not surprising conclusions,
but it's good to see evidence of them publicly

00:04:51.479 --> 00:04:54.569
every once in a while because it was not only
Donald Trump, but even some of the people

00:04:54.569 --> 00:04:59.300
around him saying it would be very, very bad
for stocks if Donald Trump were to be impeached.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:04.680
Well, he's been impeached and stocks are okay,
and of course you're not going to hear Donald

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:08.860
Trump talk about that other than on days that
stocks are up.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:13.360
Continue to take credit on days that stocks
are down claim as he did during the recent

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:14.389
NATO summit in the UK.

00:05:14.389 --> 00:05:15.389
Oh yeah.

00:05:15.389 --> 00:05:18.259
I don't, I don't really pay attention to the
stock market.

00:05:18.259 --> 00:05:23.780
Don't be tricked into believing that Donald
Trump's presence in the white house is crucial

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:25.389
for a stable stock market.

00:05:25.389 --> 00:05:29.199
And then of course, I think most of you know
and are not tricked into believing that the

00:05:29.199 --> 00:05:56.000
stock market is

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:10.830
the

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:30.639
economy for

00:06:30.639 --> 00:06:47.089
the average American worker.

